  "notes": "Revision 13 keeps the exact revision-12 atomic task: finish only the already in-flight current_code == 2 close diagnostic and capture before/after op_count, parenthesis depth, arity, argument flag and parse_ok. The new STAGE05_POSTFIX_ORACLE.md pins repository-backed grammar evidence from tests/test_parser_postfix.py: f(), f(a,b), postfix compositions and grouped postfix forms are valid; f(1 without a closing parenthesis is the case that must fail with expected ')' after arguments. Therefore a complete helper(1) may not be rejected merely because RIGHT_PAREN is encountered. Do not patch from the oracle alone; use the raw close probe to prove whether the first setter is argument-stop, call-close/depth, or post-call fallthrough/frame restoration. No new build until the current one terminates. No foreign calls, arrays, capacity changes, Stage06, canonical mutation, SELF_EMIT, Stage2, Stage3, or T4 are authorized."
